build/

# figures/generated/ holds the figure PDFs the document includes. They are
# committed, so a fresh checkout builds with latexmk alone. Rebuild them only
# after editing a figure source; see the README. The auxiliary files that
# latexmk leaves beside them are not committed.
figures/generated/*
!figures/generated/*.pdf
!figures/generated/README.md

# handbook/generated/ is committed for the same reason. It is derived from the
# ADRs, but committing it keeps the document buildable with latexmk alone, from
# a fresh checkout and on Overleaf, without make, shell scripts, or awk.
